Doom for LazyOS (the `org.lazy.doom` package)
=============================================

This package combines three works:

1. The game engine: doomgeneric (https://github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric), a port
   of Chocolate Doom, itself derived from id Software's Linux Doom source.
   Copyright (C) 1993-1996 id Software, Inc.; (C) 2005-2014 Simon Howard;
   and the doomgeneric contributors. Licensed under the GNU General Public
   License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version.

2. The LazyOS platform layer (`doom/` in the LazyOS tree): the Rust program
   that implements doomgeneric's platform hooks on the LazyOS display and
   input services. Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
   or (at your option) any later version.

   The engine is statically linked into `bin/doom.elf`, so the binary as a
   whole is distributed under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later.

3. The game data: Freedoom: Phase 1 (`resources/freedoom1.wad`,
   https://freedoom.github.io), Copyright (C) 2001-2024 the Freedoom
   contributors, under the BSD 3-Clause licence in
   `resources/COPYING-freedoom.txt`.

Corresponding source
--------------------

The complete corresponding source of `bin/doom.elf` is:

* the LazyOS tree at the revision this package was built from (`doom/`,
  `xui-app/`, `libs/messenger/`, `libs/fhs/`, `libs/generated/`,
  `tools/doom/`), and
* doomgeneric at the commit pinned in `tools/doom/fetch.py`
  (`DOOMGENERIC_REV`), fetched unmodified and compiled by `doom/build.rs`.

`python tools/doom/build.py` rebuilds the package from those two sources. The
same source is available from whoever gave you this package, on request, for
at least three years.
